rt that's when you need to  run for your life screaming I'm speaking  of screaming they're here too these have  the ability to stun our character and  summon freaky hordes in earshot of your  location will also make breakers huge  hulking mutated freaker's with immense  strength and  harder to take down like tanks I guess  on the other side of the spectrum are  the newts these are children who are  infected physically they don't have the  strength of their adult counterparts and  mentally they don't have the confidence  they are timid and follow their prey  around waiting for the right moment to  strike should we become injured in game  the newts will be on the offensive  trying to finish it off for an easy meal  I found this fact really interesting  it's possible to see swarmers and other  types of freaker's attacking newts the  freaker's are trying to survive stay  alive so they'll do that any way they  can and everyone needs to eat oh and if  you think this is ambience crowd break  is confined to the human race  think again so far we've seen infected  Ravens wolves and even this big son of a  bear expect to discover different  tactics for each encounter with the  infected the day's gun team are keeping  some mutations of the virus secret so  expect the unexpected  as more enemy types are revealed the  longer you play but of course the  infected our only one potential threat  on your travels the good old human race  remained the real problem with this  world outlaws and bandits rule the  lawless Luntz gang culture takes  precedent survival of the fittest in  full swing  the rippers are a group of enemies who  act like a cult praising the freakiest  as the next step of human evolution kind  of like the whisperers in The Walking  Dead but far more active and loud from  afar they actually look like freaker's  which can give you a fright if they pull  out a gun and start shooting  there are also Marauders and rival gangs  and settlements to attend with some are  militarized others are scavengers almost  all are hostile and we'll look to ambush  deacon in the opportune moments like a  rope to almost Decapitator x' if we  aren't paying attention the world itself  is completely open to us which makes our  motorcycle so very important  the devs describe the bike as a  character and a tool we won't be  throwing it away when we find another  this motorcycle is our motorcycle it  means a great deal to deacon this is  where a great game mechanic comes in the  motorcycle is upgradable it can be  improved incrementally upgrading the  saddlebags will allow us to carry more  items and  are the bike parts give additional  stability similarly we'll be taking care  of the bike maintaining it on the road  otherwise it's walking on foot and I've  heard it's pretty dangerous out there  something as menial as visiting a gas  station can be life or death from other  groups as you're not the only person  looking for it on a quick note nitrous  boosting is possible the narrative and  story beats in days gone have been given  extra attention learning from the  brilliance of the last of us  storytelling and horizon zero dawn  civility to make the player care  unreservedly for the main protagonist  days gone does the same in its own  unique way using flashbacks to break up  the modern day carnage to tell us more  about deacon and his family in the first  hour you'll see Deacon as a young  bachelor helping his future wife at the  roadside these small but meaningful  scenes help us understand what makes  Deacon tick his loyalty he's caring his  love of the open road everything feeds  back into modern day Deacon deacons  personal triumphs and losses impact him  and the future he tries to strive for to  simplify this we may be playing as a man  who kills thousands of free Keys and  Marauders but he wasn't this man before  the outbreak if story in videogames is  your back days gone has got you covered  another thing you're probably here for  guns lots of guns that he's gone is  packed to the nines with weapons we've  already seen pistols shotguns assault  rifles SMGs sniper rifles crossbows axes  sledge hammers baseball bats and knives  and if you're a sadist who likes to hurt  digital people in multiple ways days  gone I've got your back to lead on from  this the crafting system takes  scavenging to the next level we've seen  Deacon make a bomb with an air bag and a  few other items he's turned engine parts  into silences for weapons and as the  story progresses Deacon will have access  to other items to help craft molotovs  and improve the weapons he has in his  possession the crafting system takes  every inspiration from the last of us  which at the time was praised hugely  how do you like to play your video games  do you like stealth our all-out action  tactics are downright aggression in days  gone it's your choice if you want to sit  back and watch enemy patrol patterns  before taking them out silently go for  it if you want to set up explosives and  lead freaker's through them you can do  that too  if you prefer to run and gun then the  combat focus mechanic will be invaluable  to you  Deakin can slow down time kinda like  that scene in Red Dead Redemption design  up shots when things become too hectic  everyone loves a little bit of bullet  time thank you so much Max Payne the  developers Sony Bend have talked openly  about the dangerous open world and  stated that any second you may be  attacked the feeling of anxiety is  palpable over many years on behalf  become a minor inconvenience in video  games well not anymore  days gone brings the terror back through  the freaker's and other dynamic events  like we've seen you could be riding  happily down the road and be carotid by  a trap or even set upon by wolves the  events change and randomize to keep us  on our toes and remember if your bike  runs out of fuel you'll be stranded  pretty damn nerve-wracking the open  world is filled with checkpoints safe  houses 